   "licenseNote": "as stated in SuttaCentral publication metadata (bilara-data _publication-v2.json); the translator additionally requests that use not be for AI training datasets, AI models or AI-derived technologies",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "Regard one who sees your faults"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "as a guide to a hidden treasure."
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "Stay close to one so intelligent and astute"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "who curbs you when you need it."
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "Sticking close to such an impartial person,"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "things get better, not worse."
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "Advise and instruct;"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "curb wickedness:"
    },
    {
     "n": 9,
     "text": "for you shall be loved by the good,"
    },
    {
     "n": 10,
     "text": "and disliked by the bad."
    },
    {
     "n": 11,
     "text": "Don’t mix with bad friends,"
    },
    {
     "n": 12,
     "text": "nor with the worst of men."
    },
    {
     "n": 13,
     "text": "Mix with spiritual friends,"
    },
    {
     "n": 14,
     "text": "and with the best of men."
    },
    {
     "n": 15,
     "text": "Through joy in the teaching you sleep at ease,"
    },
    {
     "n": 16,
     "text": "with clear and confident heart."
    },
    {
     "n": 17,
     "text": "An astute person always delights in the teaching"
    },
    {
     "n": 18,
     "text": "proclaimed by the Noble One."
    },
    {
     "n": 19,
     "text": "While irrigators guide water,"
    },
    {
     "n": 20,
     "text": "fletchers bend arrows straight,"
    },
    {
     "n": 21,
     "text": "and carpenters bend timber straight,"
    },
    {
     "n": 22,
     "text": "the astute tame themselves."
    },
    {
     "n": 23,
     "text": "As the wind cannot stir"
    },
    {
     "n": 24,
     "text": "a solid mass of rock,"
    },
    {
     "n": 25,
     "text": "so too blame and praise"
    },
    {
     "n": 26,
     "text": "do not affect the wise."
    },
    {
     "n": 27,
     "text": "Like a deep lake,"
    },
    {
     "n": 28,
     "text": "clear and unclouded,"
    },
    {
     "n": 29,
     "text": "so clear are the astute"
    },
    {
     "n": 30,
     "text": "when they hear the teachings."
    },
    {
     "n": 31,
     "text": "True persons give up everything,"
    },
    {
     "n": 32,
     "text": "they don’t cajole for the things they desire."
    },
    {
     "n": 33,
     "text": "Though touched by sadness or happiness,"
    },
    {
     "n": 34,
     "text": "the astute appear neither depressed nor elated."
    },
    {
     "n": 35,
     "text": "Never wish for success by unjust means,"
    },
    {
     "n": 36,
     "text": "for your own sake or that of another,"
    },
    {
     "n": 37,
     "text": "desiring children, wealth, or nation;"
    },
    {
     "n": 38,
     "text": "rather, be virtuous, wise, and just."
    },
    {
     "n": 39,
     "text": "Few are those among humans"
    },
    {
     "n": 40,
     "text": "who cross to the far shore."
    },
    {
     "n": 41,
     "text": "The rest just run around"
    },
    {
     "n": 42,
     "text": "on the near shore."
    },
    {
     "n": 43,
     "text": "When the teaching is well explained,"
    },
    {
     "n": 44,
     "text": "the people who practice accordingly"
    },
    {
     "n": 45,
     "text": "will cross over"
    },
    {
     "n": 46,
     "text": "Death’s dominion so hard to pass."
    },
    {
     "n": 47,
     "text": "Rid of dark qualities,"
    },
    {
     "n": 48,
     "text": "an astute person would develop the bright."
    },
    {
     "n": 49,
     "text": "Having left home for homelessness"
    },
    {
     "n": 50,
     "text": "in seclusion, where joy is hard,"
    },
    {
     "n": 51,
     "text": "they’d long for satisfaction there."
    },
    {
     "n": 52,
     "text": "Forsaking sensual pleasures, owning nothing,"
    },
    {
     "n": 53,
     "text": "an astute person would cleanse themselves"
    },
    {
     "n": 54,
     "text": "of mental corruptions."
    },
    {
     "n": 55,
     "text": "And those whose minds are rightly developed"
    },
    {
     "n": 56,
     "text": "in the awakening factors;"
    },
    {
     "n": 57,
     "text": "who, letting go of attachments,"
    },
    {
     "n": 58,
     "text": "delight in not grasping:"
    },
    {
     "n": 59,
     "text": "with defilements ended, brilliant,"
    },
    {
     "n": 60,
     "text": "they are quenched in this world."
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
